# Allowlist: the house image builds one Rust binary (Dockerfile), so the context carries only what
# `cargo build --locked --release -p house-seller` reads. Everything else (the client, film, uat,
# docs, media) stays out, so a commit outside these paths no longer invalidates `COPY . .`.
# Measured over tracked files: 1396 files / 16.7 MB before, 359 files / 4.9 MB after.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.cargo
!crates
!services
# A workspace member: cargo loads its manifest and targets to resolve the workspace.
!apps/desktop/src-tauri
# include_str! in crates/table-core/src/agent.rs (release code).
!prompts

# Not re-included on purpose: rust-toolchain.toml. Its channel "1.97" is a different rustup
# toolchain from the image's 1.97.x, so carrying it made an uncached build download a second
# toolchain plus clippy and rustfmt. The FROM tag is the compiler pin.

**/target
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
